  "title": "30003439: accepted negative-curvature barrier on a nonhyperbolic cone",
  "body": "## Complete constructive solution\n\nThis affirmatively answers the original existential question.\nThe exact one-sided cone K = {(x,y,z) in R^3: x,y,z >= 0, xy^2 >= z^3}\nhas the 100-normal barrier F = -25 log[z(xy^2-z^3)], with negative\nthird-derivative curvature for every cone direction. No homogeneous\npolynomial in the original three-dimensional space has this K as its\nhyperbolicity cone. The complete analytic proof and mathematical audit\nare preserved, with the audit's optional mixed self-concordance bridge\nand explicit endpoint PSD decomposition incorporated into the proof.\nNo mathematical correction was required.\n\nThe cone is pre-existing and is credited to Hildebrand, Theorem 3.2\nfamily 5, p=3, q=3/2, under (x1,x2,x3)=(x,z,y):\nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/1305.4814\nNo novelty or priority is claimed. The broader every-regular-cone\nbarrier-existence question is not answered.\nOriginal problem: Tun\u00e7el, Oberwolfach Report 14/2017, p. 799:\nhttps://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2017/14\n\n## Distribution and review limits\n\nExactly eight authored proof/audit/acceptance/status/source-review or\npublic verification-metadata files are added under\n`unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30003439/`.\nThe independent audit records 347 successful checks and 11 rejected\nnegative controls in each of normal and optimized Python; those are\nhistorical supplementary checks, not substitutes for the universal proof.\nThe analytic verdict requires no omitted program or raw output.\n\nThis AI-assisted manuscript and audit are unrefereed. Acceptance is not\nexternal human peer review, journal acceptance or proof-assistant\ncertification. The result applies only to this one-sided cone/barrier\npair, with no signed-cone, arbitrary-exponent, duality-preservation or\nuniversal-cone claim. No exhaustive literature or priority certification\nis asserted.\n\nPrograms, raw outputs, datasets, copied third-party source documents,\nsource text/images and private coordination material are excluded.\nEdition preparation rechecked frozen byte identities and publication\nintegrity, without new scholarly retrieval, source-text inspection,\nliterature search or rerunning the original mathematical programs.\nQUEUE.md and unrelated repository files remain unchanged. No merge,\nrelease, DOI, journal submission or external outreach is requested.\n\nBase commit: `f6caddda8f8be2cdb3e91494325d8f7f365bc3fc`.\n\n## Exact distributed file identities\n\n- `ACCEPTANCE.json`: 3,698 bytes; SHA-256 `696bc54ebb47bdc9045b0b54bd8d4e14dea69662afc1cfc74f2a1ca8425a99e6`.\n- `MANIFEST.json`: 1,596 bytes; SHA-256 `d522e68aa6a54b710d1a9b891ada86fa9d9ddacd7d1302803e191183e33dbe52`.\n- `MATHEMATICAL_AUDIT.md`: 21,047 bytes; SHA-256 `b1be3112c8f193c26ead211bdaa03f98c2a7422603162f2bde402aa410d4423f`.\n- `PROOF.md`: 13,923 bytes; SHA-256 `9577476ee2c0fd2e3d12ab1265201d8b99f6ef50a9060e245c46f872dd673302`.\n- `README.md`: 2,964 bytes; SHA-256 `fc6b4fb5298aec26658b2877e54f03e3126e896c4c9de1e8c789912949ab5444`.\n- `SOURCE_METADATA.json`: 7,521 bytes; SHA-256 `52af60ab2ad2e5f907d50d06135aaeca03e755b3220ef08e2063d0b7771492d3`.\n- `SOURCE_REVIEW.md`: 3,343 bytes; SHA-256 `a1c1b76807cbf261f5c9be6c9c64a2c9a32657cadec3524974f07b7b2e6d3998`.\n- `STATUS.json`: 1,837 bytes; SHA-256 `772e06968971f38ebedcc791d651b6bfdf9a8b478a1a7f26c557dcca10d9f8a5`.\n\nThe manifest lists eight members and hashes the other seven; this body pins the manifest independently.\n",
